      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T18:01:38Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "So these profiles eventually map to some sub profiles such as HighPerformance or ProcessCapacityHigh https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/core/libprocessgroup/profiles/task_profiles.json;l\u003d651?q\u003dSCHED_SP_COMPUTE\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain\n\nWhich eventually just maps to the \"foreground\" cgroup, which if we check on a device maps to all the cores except the 2 highest performance cores on panther for example. With --host-cpu-topology and --virt-cpufreq, the guest will decide which core it places on based on vcpu, whereas the current task-profile will limit the tasks from using the 2 largest cores.\n\n```\ncat /dev/cpuset/foreground/effective_cpus\n0-5\n```",
